Rebased onto current main (9691e711). The source change is unchanged, and so is the crash path: `release_memory_occupation()` still pauses the KV-cache tag before `flush_cache()`, and the flush now reaches `ShortConvPool.clear()` and `NGramPool.clear()` through `StateStorage.clear()` (#46980). The 8x H20 check in the description was run on the September base.

I updated the one test that #46980 and #43439 broke: its pool stub now goes through `StateStorage`, and it no longer expects `clear()` to zero `req_generation`. On CPU against the rebased tree, the 6 new tests pass; reverting only the source makes the 3 offload-safety tests fail, each by touching the offloaded storage; the rest of `test/registered/unit/mem_cache/` shows no new failures; pre-commit passes.

@ispobock @xiezhq-hermann, could one of you add the `run-ci` label when you have a moment? No CI has run on this PR yet. Thanks!

